## Context

`tickets/AGENTS.md` is not a harness file. It is an asset embedded in the `erg`
binary (`git-erg/src/go/assets/AGENTS.md`), written by `erg init`, and — this is
the part that makes the drift load-bearing — **force-overwritten by
`erg migrate`**, deliberately: `git-erg/src/go/migrate_test.go:448` asserts
"a diverged AGENTS.md IS force-overwritten by migrateLayout (charter
behaviour)". The harness has been editing it as if it owned it.

Measured 2026-09-10, on `origin/main`:

| copy | chars | md5 |
|------|-------|-----|
| shipped asset `git-erg/src/go/assets/AGENTS.md` | 2 141 | `b622d4f0…` |
| nine adopter repos (DOIfetch, git-erg, search-works-for-zotero, aedist, archiveCIRED, climate-finance-het, padme, polycentric_activity, zoteus-fts5) | 2 141 | `b622d4f0…` |
| `chemin-de-voix` | 1 388 | `5383a736…` |
| **this repo** | **7 969** | `3ea9ab0b…` |

The asset was last changed 2026-06-18. The harness copy has been changed five
times since (2026-07-11 → 2026-09-01), every one of them additive, and none of
them propagated. Three consequences, in increasing order of cost.

**1. The harness's local rules are unbacked.** The 5.8 KB the harness added —
the optimistic-ID discipline, the renumber-clear-of-the-frontier rule, the
`gh pr view` scan, the decision-records-vs-artifacts split — is exactly the
material `erg migrate` is chartered to delete. Nothing warns, and the deletion
would look like a routine tool run.

**2. Nine repos are resident-loading two claims the harness has disproved.**
The shipped template still says `tickets/erg-github` adds a `verify` check that
fails a PR referencing a still-open ticket — the harness deleted that as
fiction on 2026-07-12 (`9703af3`). It also still says "on ID collision,
renumber to the next free ID" — reversed here on 2026-07-27 after one filing
collided three times in one session, refined 2026-09-01. `climate-finance-het`
and `search-works-for-zotero`, the two repos whose incidents produced the
correction, are among the nine still being told the wrong thing. And
`chemin-de-voix` is a pre-0175 fossil below even that: `Tag:` for `Label:`, and
a U+FFFD where `≤` was — the corruption git-erg fixed on 2026-05-29.

**3. It is a resident body outside the resident-body gate.** `AGENTS.md`
reaches every session through `@tickets/AGENTS.md` in `CLAUDE.md`, a fact
`rules/README.md` states explicitly. At 7 969 chars it is ~2 000 tokens per
session, +22% on top of the 35 926-char gated set whose remaining headroom is
74 chars. `tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py` scopes to `RULES = REPO /
"rules"`, so none of its three invariants reach it. Applying them by hand:

- `test_resident_rules_carry_no_ticket_numbers` — **would fail**, 2 hits
  (`ticket 0321`, `ticket 0243`).
- `test_resident_rules_ship_no_shell_recipes` — **would pass while the file
  carries a shell recipe.** `SHELL_FENCE` anchors the opening fence at column
  zero; the block at `AGENTS.md:41-45` is indented two spaces under a list item.
  Measured against that known-positive: anchored 0 hits, `^\s*`-relaxed 1 hit.
  That blind spot is independent of this ticket and applies to `rules/**` too.

## Relevant files

- `tickets/AGENTS.md` — the forked copy, 7 969 chars
- `rules/README.md` — names AGENTS.md as resident-by-another-path; the exclusion is stated, never defended
- `tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py` — the three 0572 invariants, scoped to `rules/`; `SHELL_FENCE` carries the anchoring blind spot
- `~/CNRS/code/git-erg/src/go/assets/AGENTS.md` — upstream source of truth (cross-repo)
- `~/CNRS/code/git-erg/src/go/migrate_test.go:448` — the force-overwrite charter

## Decision the author owns

Where does each rule live? The partition is architectural, not editorial, and
the work cannot start without it:

- **(a) Upstream everything durable.** Push the collision discipline, the scan
  and the artifacts/decision-records split into the git-erg asset, cut the
  harness copy back to the shipped text, let `erg update` redistribute. One
  source of truth; the incident narrative has to survive the trip or be
  demoted to memory notes first.
- **(b) Split by layer.** Tool-invariant rules (`%erg 0.1` format, log verbs,
  atomic IDs, artifacts by reference) upstream; harness-local practice
  (`gh pr view` scans, the frontier rule, CI job names) moves out of
  `AGENTS.md` into `rules/` where the gate already reaches it. This is what
  `feedback_layer_correctness` and the 0572 precedent both point at, and it is
  the recommended default.
- **(c) Keep the fork, defend it.** Declare the harness copy authoritative,
  teach `erg migrate` to leave it alone, and extend the budget gate to cover
  it. Costs a git-erg change either way, and leaves nine adopters stale.

Under (a) or (b) the git-erg half is a separate ticket **filed in git-erg's own
store**, per `feedback_cross_repo_tickets_live_at_destination`; this ticket
stays open as its tracker until both halves land.

## Actions

1. Get the author's verdict on (a)/(b)/(c). Everything below assumes (b).
2. File the git-erg child: correct the two disproved claims in
   `src/go/assets/AGENTS.md` (drop the `erg-github` verify sentence; replace
   "renumber to the next free ID" with the frontier rule), bump the asset, and
   say how the nine adopters pick it up (`erg update`, or a per-repo `erg init`
   refresh) — including `chemin-de-voix`, which needs the 0175 `Label:` rename
   and the U+FFFD repair it never received.
3. In this repo, move harness-local practice out of `tickets/AGENTS.md` into
   the rules tree, respecting the resident budget: the shell recipe goes to the
   script or skill that runs it, the two ticket numbers become named memory
   pointers, the dated incident narrative goes to memory notes cited by name.
4. Cut `tickets/AGENTS.md` back to the shipped asset plus only what genuinely
   belongs to the ticket store's format.
5. Extend the gate: cover `tickets/AGENTS.md` in
   `tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py` (or a sibling), and let `SHELL_FENCE`
   tolerate leading whitespace so an indented recipe is visible.

## Test

Red step, before any prose moves: extend
`tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py` so `tickets/AGENTS.md` is in the measured
set and the `SHELL_FENCE` regex tolerates leading whitespace. Both new
assertions must fail against the current tree — the ticket-number one on
`ticket 0321`/`ticket 0243`, the shell one on the indented block at line 41 —
and the shell one must also still pass on today's `rules/**`, so the relaxation
is proved to change only what it should.

## Verification

- [ ] `md5sum` of `tickets/AGENTS.md` matches the shipped asset, or the diff
      is a reviewed list of format rules the asset does not carry
- [ ] a grep for the `erg-github` verify sentence and for "next free ID"
      returns nothing across all ten adopter copies and the asset
- [ ] `chemin-de-voix` copy carries `Label:` and no U+FFFD byte (`EF BF BD`)
- [ ] the extended budget test is red before the trim and green after
- [ ] `uv run pytest -m adherence` green

## Invariants

- No rule currently in `tickets/AGENTS.md` is lost — each is either upstreamed,
  relocated to `rules/`, or demoted to a memory note that something cites
- The gated resident total stays under `RESIDENT_BUDGET`; relocating prose into
  `rules/` without trimming it just moves the cost inside the gate
- `erg check tickets/` stays green; no adopter repo is edited from this repo's
  worktree

## Exit criteria

- Author's verdict recorded in this ticket's log
- git-erg child filed at the destination and referenced here
- `tickets/AGENTS.md` in this repo no longer forks silently: either it matches
  the asset, or a test fails when it stops matching
- Both disproved claims gone from every copy on this machine
- This tracker closes only after the git-erg child merges and the ten copies
  are re-checksummed
